Z||000001||Old Lar||10-15-2000||07:42 AM||||I can only guess it may be similiar to "Quicken" " a money management program.<P>I use "Quicken" and it helps keeping track of my checking account and investments.  I rely on it to know when to pay the bills, but it does take some time to enter your information. Remember GIGO..garbage in, garbage out.  If not done right and kept current it is pretty worthless.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||10-15-2000||07:11 PM||||I use it, and I like it. I have online banking and every couple of days I download a file from the internet and import it to MS MONEY. It keeps track of my checking and savings and CD's. I just like using it to keep an offline record of my purchases. It is just like quicken.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-15-2000||10:53 PM||||Unlike quicken it is a Microsoft product with god knows how many security holes. A new hole is found in office and/or windows about every 2 weeks.<P>You also need to look into what if any charges your bank has for using it. Most banks have either a minum deposit requirement or a fee associated with online banking.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||10-15-2000||11:03 PM||||Yeah, but I wouldnt be to worried about a security problem. Unless your going to be managing huge amonts of money on there, also, just to be safe, I dont enter my account numbers on there. If it requires on, I would use a fake one, just to be safe. If your interested in the online banking thing, make sure your bank provides the info in a format importable to MSMONEY. My online banking is free, but if you want to use the online billpay, you pay!<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
